developer/amix/sysroot

The files in this package are the usr/ tree of Amiga UNIX (AMIX) 2.1c at
patch level 2a, as Commodore shipped it and an installation made it, taken
unchanged from https://github.com/amigaux/amix-system (the commit is named
in /opt/m68k-amix-sysroot/etc/amix-sysroot.release).  That repository
states:

    Amiga Corporation approved releasing Amiga UNIX on 2026-09-23, and these
    files are published under that approval. They are not covered by amix's
    MIT licence.

    Amiga UNIX is Commodore's port of AT&T UNIX System V Release 4; portions
    are copyright AT&T, UNIX System Laboratories and their successors.

    This site and its developers are not affiliated with, endorsed by, or
    sponsored by Amiga Corporation. Amiga is a registered trademark of Amiga
    Corporation.

The same applies to this package: it is not affiliated with, endorsed by or
sponsored by Amiga Corporation.  Amiga is a registered trademark of Amiga
Corporation; UNIX is a registered trademark of The Open Group.

The only changes made by this package: absolute symbolic links were made
relative to the sysroot, and the marker file etc/amix-sysroot.release was
added (written by the package build, no licensed content).
